WEBVTT

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.390
As the sizzling heat continues,

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:08.510
hordes of beachgoers have
flocked here to Oarai Beach.

00:00:09.420 --> 00:00:12.400
When I was a kid, I thought Oarai Beach

00:00:12.820 --> 00:00:16.030
was "Owarai", or laughter, Beach.

00:00:16.410 --> 00:00:18.950
That would be a bizarre place.

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:21.800
Your thought process is what's bizarre here.

00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:25.170
Speaking of which, I haven't been to the beach yet this year.

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:26.250
Actually...

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:30.460
I ain't never seen the ocean in my life.

00:00:31.630 --> 00:00:34.170
You've <i>never</i> seen the ocean?

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:36.180
Mino-poyo, are you serious?

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:40.140
You haven't even been there once?

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:43.180
Not with Gifu bein' landlocked and all.

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:45.140
Not even on a field trip?

00:00:45.730 --> 00:00:48.820
In elementary school we
visited Kyoto and Nara,

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:52.290
and in middle school it was
Kyoto and Nara again.

00:00:52.290 --> 00:00:54.950
Sounds like you were screwed over by regional interests.

00:00:55.610 --> 00:00:57.160
Fine, then.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.400
Let's go to the beach!

00:00:59.400 --> 00:01:02.740
We can make room in
our schedules for a day trip.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:04.200
Darn tootin'!

00:01:04.200 --> 00:01:06.250
Let's mosey down to the
beach our next day off!

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:08.210
The beach!

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:10.710
Featuring Ringo in a swimsuit...

00:01:11.710 --> 00:01:13.210
Ringo in a swimsuit...

00:01:14.360 --> 00:01:15.970
and Ringo in a swimsuit!

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:17.970
This is sounding better and better!

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:19.590
It'll be a trip to remember!

00:01:19.590 --> 00:01:20.850
Quite so.

00:01:20.850 --> 00:01:22.180
Summer vacation's only once a year!

00:01:22.180 --> 00:01:23.430
Let's have some fun!

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.100
<i>And when the day came...</i>

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.110
The incredibly powerful
Typhoon Number 9

00:01:31.110 --> 00:01:35.030
has made landfall in the Tokai region with no signs of slowing down.

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:37.490
We gots hit with a typhoon.

00:03:11.530 --> 00:03:16.210
Heavy rain, flooding, high wind, lightning,
and landslide warnings for the Minotamo area.

00:03:16.210 --> 00:03:18.710
That's a <i>mangan</i>. 12,000 points.

00:03:18.710 --> 00:03:20.760
We've got a full course of
weather on the menu.

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:26.300
With a storm surge or high surf warning we'd have a <i>haneman</i>, 18,000 points.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:27.560
But we're landlocked.

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:29.570
And it's not just the typhoon.

00:03:29.570 --> 00:03:32.120
We've had cloudbursts every evening.

00:03:32.120 --> 00:03:34.060
The summers around here
are pretty temperamental.

00:03:34.370 --> 00:03:40.740
Wanna go beach! Wanna go beach! Wanna go beach!

00:03:40.740 --> 00:03:42.450
Not as temperamental as <i>someone</i>.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.820
We were gonna get wet anyway!

00:03:44.820 --> 00:03:47.200
The rain ain't no 'count!

00:03:47.200 --> 00:03:50.720
Go beach! Wanna go beach!

00:03:50.720 --> 00:03:52.120
Be realistic.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:55.250
The trains and buses are stopped. How do you plan to go?

00:03:55.250 --> 00:03:56.540
Then I'll go by bike!

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:58.040
Bring-bring!

00:03:57.150 --> 00:03:58.770
Now that's just asking to get hurt!

00:03:58.770 --> 00:04:00.380
You'll be blown away, bike and all.

00:04:00.380 --> 00:04:03.050
Just give it up already.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:07.300
I'll take you anywhere you want
some other time to make up for it.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:08.350
Anywhere?

00:04:08.350 --> 00:04:09.850
Yes, anywhere.

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:11.060
Got somewhere in mind?

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:14.100
Yeah! Actually, I've been hankerin' to go to—

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:17.230
It's on the offensive,
and with incredible force!

00:04:18.060 --> 00:04:19.190
Y-You!

00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:21.230
Money Kanegami!

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:22.490
What brings you here?

00:04:22.490 --> 00:04:25.410
I had a practical class,

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:28.530
but thanks to the typhoon, no one else came.

00:04:28.530 --> 00:04:30.370
Neither the buses nor trains are running,

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:33.410
and the roads are flooded,
so our teacher had to turn back.

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:35.170
So your class is canceled?

00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:36.710
Yep.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:41.050
On top of that, I'm now stranded.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:43.380
If you don't mind, I'm gonna crash here for a bit.

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:45.680
No problem. I mean, given the circumstances.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:48.050
Money-san, what was your class going to do?

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.600
Transplant the cymbidiums to the mountains.

00:04:49.600 --> 00:04:51.810
Cymbi... um... plant-plant?

00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:54.850
The cymbidium. It's a kind of orchid.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:57.190
They grow at high altitudes in Southeast Asia

00:04:57.190 --> 00:04:59.520
and prefer dry, cool climates.

00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:03.070
So we have to move them to the mountains in the summer, or we'll get bud blast.

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:05.930
Synchronized...

00:05:03.740 --> 00:05:05.900
"Bud blast"? What's that?

00:05:05.900 --> 00:05:08.920
A kind of abnormal growth caused by excessive heat.

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:09.730
High dive! Whoo! Splash!

00:05:08.920 --> 00:05:11.040
Once it happens, the flowers are worthless.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.790
Wow, you know your stuff. Are you big on flowers?

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:15.040
Take that!

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:15.620
Flowers make money.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:16.290
That explains it.

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:20.590
Back in the day, a pot of these bad boys
could run for millions of yen.

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:23.880
The root of all evil has never looked so good.

00:05:23.880 --> 00:05:29.720
We were gonna load the cymbies on the minibus today.

00:05:29.720 --> 00:05:31.640
Y-You mean <i>that</i> bus?

00:05:31.640 --> 00:05:33.520
It takes a certain kind of courage to board that thing.

00:05:34.270 --> 00:05:38.400
Well, with this weather,
it's not the cymbies

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.230
but the greenhouses we
should be worried about.

00:05:41.230 --> 00:05:41.980
No kidding.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:44.900
Kousaku, shouldn't we close the storm shutters?

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:46.570
The wind could send things flying.

00:05:46.570 --> 00:05:47.700
Right, good idea.

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:51.980
Holy cow.

00:05:53.700 --> 00:05:55.250
It's certainly quite impressive.

00:05:55.250 --> 00:05:56.290
It's like...

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:56.790
It's like...

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:58.830
the school grounds...

00:05:58.830 --> 00:05:59.750
The grounds...

00:06:00.830 --> 00:06:02.210
have turned into an ocean.

00:06:02.210 --> 00:06:04.550
Ocean?!

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:05.550
Oh, crap!

00:06:05.550 --> 00:06:06.840
Restrain Minori!

00:06:06.840 --> 00:06:08.800
Use whatever force necessary!

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:12.430
Beach Boys!

00:06:16.430 --> 00:06:17.980
Freedom!

00:06:17.980 --> 00:06:19.100
Minori!

00:06:19.100 --> 00:06:20.730
It's dangerous out there! Come back!

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:21.730
Kou-tan, it's the ocean!

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:22.980
The honest-to-goodness ocean!

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:24.380
Come on in!

00:06:25.110 --> 00:06:27.360
That's <i>not</i> the ocean, it's the school...

00:06:28.900 --> 00:06:29.740
Dang, this is fun!

00:06:29.740 --> 00:06:31.360
Kou-tan!

00:06:31.360 --> 00:06:32.990
Whoa, the waves! The waves!

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:33.920
That idiot!

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:36.080
What's "fun" about this crazy storm?!

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:39.040
So much fun!

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:41.250
How?

00:06:41.250 --> 00:06:43.960
So much fun!

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:45.960
What is?

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:48.970
So much fun!

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:50.550
Yeah, right.

00:06:51.010 --> 00:06:52.800
There's no way...

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:53.550
it's fun...

00:06:54.550 --> 00:06:55.350
Fun...

00:06:57.520 --> 00:07:01.940
So... So much fun!

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:03.980
Take that!

00:07:03.980 --> 00:07:05.400
Oh no, you don't!

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:07.860
Come and get me!

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:16.450
Me too!

00:07:39.560 --> 00:07:41.770
It's just mud, so it's fine, right?

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:43.400
That's right. It's mud.

00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:46.480
Whatever anyone else may say, it's mud.

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:48.730
Then it's all right if I squint while I watch?

00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:50.610
Yes, just for a little while.

00:07:50.610 --> 00:07:52.650
Let's play beach volleyball!

00:07:52.650 --> 00:07:53.990
Kousaku, fetch a beach ball!

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:55.950
Right-o!

00:07:57.580 --> 00:07:59.040
And go!

00:08:02.710 --> 00:08:04.920
And that's the game!

00:08:05.920 --> 00:08:07.710
Next, let's split a watermelon!

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:08.900
Kei, the watermelon!

00:08:08.900 --> 00:08:10.260
Right away!

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.970
And done!

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:19.600
Next up, barbecue!

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:21.350
I'm on it!

00:08:24.270 --> 00:08:25.900
It won't light.

00:08:25.900 --> 00:08:27.270
Bring the kerosene!

00:08:27.270 --> 00:08:28.650
Hoo-hah!

00:08:30.360 --> 00:08:32.070
And light!

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:37.070
Barbe...cue?

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:38.870
Campfire!

00:08:38.870 --> 00:08:39.740
Well, close enough!

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:41.700
Fire!

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:43.810
This would be better with music!

00:08:43.810 --> 00:08:45.420
All right! Gimme a sec!

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:47.710
Let's see, something with a summer vibe!

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:53.130
Let's dance!

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:00.640
What's with this preposterous racket?!

00:09:01.260 --> 00:09:03.480
You're scaring the cows!

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:04.480
Yoshida-san!

00:09:04.480 --> 00:09:06.270
Hey, guys! The jiggling wonder is here!

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:10.020
Wh-What is the meaning of this?!

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:12.980
Come on, get out of those stuffy work clothes!

00:09:12.980 --> 00:09:15.200
We're at the beach, don'tcha see?

00:09:15.200 --> 00:09:16.650
Unhand me, you filth!

00:09:16.650 --> 00:09:18.280
I'm serious! Let go!

00:09:18.280 --> 00:09:21.830
Well looky here, gal!
You even got your swimsuit on!

00:09:21.830 --> 00:09:23.950
A white bikini? You know what's up!

00:09:23.950 --> 00:09:26.660
N-No! This isn't a swimsuit, it's my und—

00:09:26.660 --> 00:09:29.670
Nipple slip! Nipple slip!

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:30.210
That's right!

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:31.880
Nipple slip!

00:09:34.090 --> 00:09:35.550
Hold it right there!

00:09:37.380 --> 00:09:40.180
Frenzied revelry on a sacred beach?

00:09:40.180 --> 00:09:43.220
The lifeguards may allow it, but we will not!

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:44.430
Who are you?!

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:50.360
The Tamo Agriculture and Forestry High School beach volleyball team!

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:53.110
Beach volleyball team?!

00:09:53.110 --> 00:09:55.570
A beach volleyball team
in a landlocked prefecture?

00:09:55.570 --> 00:09:58.400
That makes as much sense
as a bobsled team in Jamaica.

00:09:58.400 --> 00:10:00.800
So what does the beach
volleyball team want with us?

00:10:00.800 --> 00:10:03.700
For your information, we're not gonna stop stripping Yoshida-san!

00:10:03.700 --> 00:10:05.580
And I have no intention of stopping you.

00:10:05.580 --> 00:10:06.330
Hey!

00:10:06.330 --> 00:10:08.920
Let's first get the introductions out of the way.

00:10:08.920 --> 00:10:11.920
I'm the team captain, Nice Guy Hamaoka.

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:12.790
And this here...

00:10:12.790 --> 00:10:14.920
Butter! Butter!

00:10:16.590 --> 00:10:18.420
Don't tell me he's...

00:10:18.420 --> 00:10:19.430
Butter Ken?!

00:10:19.430 --> 00:10:21.090
Kousaku, do you know him?

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:22.350
Nope, not at all!

00:10:22.350 --> 00:10:23.680
Never heard of the guy!

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:26.220
I have no idea that he's a Bioengineering student

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:30.140
majoring in food production with a focus on sweets
who specializes in Western confections!

00:10:30.140 --> 00:10:31.810
I prefer rice in the mornings!

00:10:31.810 --> 00:10:34.070
Butter Ken!

00:10:34.070 --> 00:10:34.690
Oh, just shut up!

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:37.070
We challenge you to a match!

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:37.650
A match?

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:40.910
We've been training for
the inter-high competition.

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:43.370
We'd like to use this opportunity to practice as much as possible!

00:10:45.580 --> 00:10:47.460
So where are they holding the competition?

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:48.330
Nagano.

00:10:48.330 --> 00:10:50.080
That's also landlocked!
And right next door!

00:10:50.080 --> 00:10:53.210
It may be the national championship, but we plan to make it a day trip.

00:10:53.210 --> 00:10:54.380
So where was it last year?

00:10:54.380 --> 00:10:55.500
Gunma.

00:10:55.500 --> 00:10:56.380
You poor bastards!

00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:58.670
And the year before was in Saitama!

00:10:58.670 --> 00:11:02.090
Neither Gifu, Nagano, Gunma, nor Saitama are by the ocean.

00:11:02.090 --> 00:11:03.600
Where was the competition held?

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:04.690
On a riverbank!

00:11:04.690 --> 00:11:05.810
God, that must hurt.

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:07.960
Anyway, we challenge you!

00:11:07.960 --> 00:11:09.020
I mean, please play us!

00:11:09.560 --> 00:11:10.940
We beg of you!

00:11:11.600 --> 00:11:13.400
Got a moment, chief?

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:14.480
What is it, Kanegami?

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:16.730
The paddies are in trouble.

00:11:22.150 --> 00:11:23.780
"Trouble" is right.

00:11:29.730 --> 00:11:31.000
Hurry up, guys!

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:32.550
If we don't act, the paddies will submerge!

00:11:32.550 --> 00:11:34.260
Kousaku, what do you mean, submerge?

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:36.540
The water level will rise above the tops of the plants!

00:11:37.020 --> 00:11:39.270
Paddies are meant to be
flooded up to the stems,

00:11:39.270 --> 00:11:42.630
but if the water reaches the ears,
they'll start to bud!

00:11:42.630 --> 00:11:43.280
Bud?

00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:46.260
Once that happens, we won't be able to eat or sell the crop anymore!

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:47.780
It won't even be useful as seed rice!

00:11:47.780 --> 00:11:49.780
All our effort will have gone to waste!

00:11:49.780 --> 00:11:50.480
Oh, no!

00:12:02.200 --> 00:12:03.270
What now?

00:12:03.270 --> 00:12:05.280
What should we do, Kousaku?

00:12:05.280 --> 00:12:08.080
Don't worry, I'll... I'll think of something!

00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:11.730
Kou-tan!

00:12:11.730 --> 00:12:12.830
Kousaku!

00:12:13.270 --> 00:12:15.540
If only we had noticed earlier.

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:17.500
Cease your panic, insects!

00:12:18.200 --> 00:12:19.640
Have all your—

00:12:19.640 --> 00:12:20.710
Just a second!

00:12:23.130 --> 00:12:24.050
Take two!

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:26.800
Three, two, one, go!

00:12:28.220 --> 00:12:30.060
What do you think you're doing?!

00:12:30.830 --> 00:12:32.370
Cease your panic, insects!

00:12:32.370 --> 00:12:33.520
Oh, we're starting from there?

00:12:34.060 --> 00:12:37.430
Have all your practical lessons taught you nothing?

00:12:37.430 --> 00:12:39.480
You dare call yourselves agricultural students?

00:12:41.440 --> 00:12:44.480
Hata Kousaku, you take command!

00:12:44.480 --> 00:12:47.320
I and the others will follow your lead!

00:12:47.320 --> 00:12:48.280
Do I make myself clear?

00:12:48.280 --> 00:12:49.200
Brassiere!

00:12:49.200 --> 00:12:50.200
What happened to "roger"?!

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:51.330
All right.

00:12:51.330 --> 00:12:52.800
First we need to open the rear gate.

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:54.050
Kei, you're up!

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:02.520
Rear gate?

00:13:02.520 --> 00:13:03.840
That's the drainage gate.

00:13:03.840 --> 00:13:05.650
We're going to let the water out.

00:13:05.650 --> 00:13:07.720
If it's open, the plants won't submerge?

00:13:08.040 --> 00:13:10.350
As long as the wind doesn't blow them down.

00:13:14.270 --> 00:13:16.480
Here I go!

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:25.350
Kamatori-kun!

00:13:25.350 --> 00:13:26.840
Kei, are you okay?

00:13:26.840 --> 00:13:27.650
I'm fine!

00:13:27.650 --> 00:13:29.870
Our bigger concern is the mud!

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:35.250
This drain's not gonna clog on my watch!

00:13:35.680 --> 00:13:39.120
All right, while Kei buys us time, we need to rope off the paddies!

00:13:39.120 --> 00:13:39.710
Got it!

00:13:47.180 --> 00:13:48.800
Don't try to rush!

00:13:48.800 --> 00:13:50.300
You'll cause more damage if you fall!

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:53.810
Hamaoka-san! Head back to the dorms
and bring more rope!

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:54.180
Understood!

00:13:54.180 --> 00:13:56.680
Yoshida-san, your boobs
are crushing the rice!

00:13:57.100 --> 00:13:58.770
Minori, get the junk in your trunk
outta the way!

00:13:58.770 --> 00:14:01.190
Ringo, keep up the good work!

00:14:02.360 --> 00:14:05.530
Butter Ken, I think your speedo
got washed off. Do you need help?

00:14:05.530 --> 00:14:08.450
Butter repels water, so I'm all good!

00:14:08.450 --> 00:14:09.530
Butter's really something!

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:22.460
All right, hopefully this will hold.

00:14:22.460 --> 00:14:24.300
That just leaves Class D's.

00:14:24.300 --> 00:14:25.510
Hata Kousaku!

00:14:25.510 --> 00:14:26.960
What is it, Yoshida-san?

00:14:28.170 --> 00:14:30.720
The rice in Class D's paddy has matured too quickly!

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:35.260
The ears are too heavy for the ropes to support!

00:14:35.260 --> 00:14:36.520
Collapse is inevitable!

00:14:36.890 --> 00:14:38.640
Why is it only Class D?

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:40.020
Kanegami, don't tell me...

00:14:41.480 --> 00:14:42.480
I'm sorry.

00:14:42.980 --> 00:14:44.190
It's Koshihikari.

00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:46.570
Why did you plant <i>that</i>?

00:14:46.570 --> 00:14:47.570
What's wrong with it?

00:14:47.570 --> 00:14:51.280
Koshihikari is infamous for
how easily the plants fall down.

00:14:51.280 --> 00:14:52.780
The plants are simply too tall!

00:14:54.330 --> 00:14:56.490
What's worse, the ears are already drooping.

00:14:56.490 --> 00:14:59.750
There's no way they'll
stand up to this wind!

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:00.460
Oh, no!

00:15:00.870 --> 00:15:03.080
Why the heck did you plant
such a high-maintenance breed?

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:06.550
What was I supposed to do? Koshihikari sells the best!

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:09.090
Well, have fun selling them
after the plants collapse!

00:15:09.470 --> 00:15:11.000
Will you peons stop bickering?

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:12.590
What use is quibbling now?

00:15:13.300 --> 00:15:17.330
Nothing is impossible for the
Aramis Navy or Tamo Agricultural!

00:15:17.330 --> 00:15:18.060
We can't give up yet!

00:15:18.850 --> 00:15:21.770
There must... be some way...

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:30.440
There's no way we can transport the plants.

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:33.160
Which means we need to block the wind.

00:15:33.430 --> 00:15:35.620
But... how?

00:15:35.970 --> 00:15:36.780
I know!

00:15:36.780 --> 00:15:38.790
How about the beach volleyball net?

00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:40.330
Good luck stopping
<i>wind</i> with that!

00:15:40.660 --> 00:15:42.460
We need something more solid!

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:45.500
But Kou-tan, we ain't got the time
for a sandbag barrier.

00:15:45.500 --> 00:15:46.540
I'm not stupid, you kn—

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:49.050
That's it!

00:15:49.050 --> 00:15:50.740
Kanegami! The keys!

00:15:51.720 --> 00:15:53.760
The keys to the minibus!

00:15:54.140 --> 00:15:56.720
The one you were gonna move the cymbidiums with!

00:15:58.100 --> 00:16:00.310
What do you have in mind, chief?

00:16:01.560 --> 00:16:02.890
There's no time to explain!

00:16:02.890 --> 00:16:05.190
The rest of you, rope off Class D's paddy!

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:16.280
This might do the trick.

00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:18.370
Kousaku?

00:16:18.370 --> 00:16:19.870
Ringo? What about the roping?

00:16:20.950 --> 00:16:22.330
The others are handling it.

00:16:22.710 --> 00:16:27.210
Boobs-san wasn't sure you could manage alone, so she sent me.

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:29.880
She has such faith in me.

00:16:29.880 --> 00:16:31.210
<i>Nice going, Boobs.</i>

00:16:33.010 --> 00:16:35.130
So what's your plan?

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:36.970
We're gonna create a barrier.

00:16:36.970 --> 00:16:37.890
A barrier?

00:16:37.890 --> 00:16:40.140
We'll move the bus upwind
to deflect the storm.

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:43.890
Class D's paddy is the furthest upwind,

00:16:43.890 --> 00:16:46.980
which means three of the four sides are roads.

00:16:46.980 --> 00:16:49.820
If we move the bus so it's against the wind,

00:16:49.820 --> 00:16:52.400
it'll create a barrier and protect the paddies!

00:16:54.570 --> 00:16:57.070
But Kousaku, can you drive?

00:16:57.070 --> 00:16:58.910
It's a diesel stick shift, right?

00:16:58.910 --> 00:16:59.530
In that case...

00:17:02.200 --> 00:17:03.960
it should work the same as a tractor!

00:17:09.090 --> 00:17:11.550
Shift to first gear.

00:17:12.130 --> 00:17:14.510
Release the parking brake.

00:17:16.300 --> 00:17:21.100
Slowly give the engine some gas, and start moving at half clutch.

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:25.350
Once in motion, release the clutch,

00:17:27.140 --> 00:17:28.270
and step on the accelerator!

00:17:32.280 --> 00:17:34.360
Yes! I did it without stalling!

00:17:34.360 --> 00:17:35.400
That was amazing!

00:17:35.400 --> 00:17:37.450
Nah, it was nothing.

00:17:38.570 --> 00:17:39.280
But...

00:17:39.280 --> 00:17:40.200
But?

00:17:40.740 --> 00:17:44.660
Driving without a teacher's permission is against school rules.

00:17:45.000 --> 00:17:47.830
I'll probably get chewed out.

00:17:47.830 --> 00:17:49.380
This could be my second suspension.

00:17:55.090 --> 00:17:56.090
It's okay.

00:17:57.680 --> 00:18:00.180
I'll share the blame.

00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:09.690
Here we go, Ringo!

00:18:25.160 --> 00:18:26.330
What the heck?!

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:27.870
I can't see a thing!

00:18:27.870 --> 00:18:29.500
Kousaku, start the wipers!

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:30.880
Wi... pers?

00:18:30.880 --> 00:18:32.790
Those things that wipe the rain
from the windshield!

00:18:37.080 --> 00:18:38.300
The bus must have them!

00:18:39.090 --> 00:18:40.370
Kousaku!

00:18:43.970 --> 00:18:45.430
I have no idea.

00:18:45.890 --> 00:18:49.810
Neither tractors nor combines have wipers!

00:18:49.810 --> 00:18:50.390
Augh!

00:18:55.360 --> 00:18:56.740
Hey, what are you—

00:18:56.740 --> 00:18:57.570
Keep driving!

00:18:57.900 --> 00:18:59.780
I'll watch where we're going.

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:02.110
Just follow my directions.

00:19:02.110 --> 00:19:03.240
Huh? O-Okay...

00:19:03.700 --> 00:19:05.450
Keep going straight!

00:19:06.870 --> 00:19:07.660
Got it!

00:19:08.080 --> 00:19:09.540
Now a slight right!

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:11.040
We're passing the gym!

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:12.080
Okay!

00:19:19.130 --> 00:19:21.220
Turn straight again!

00:19:21.680 --> 00:19:24.430
Slowly... Slowly...

00:19:42.150 --> 00:19:43.200
It's Kousaku!

00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:45.280
We're coming up on the sharp right!

00:19:45.280 --> 00:19:45.910
Ready?

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:46.660
Ready!

00:19:47.160 --> 00:19:50.290
Three... two... one...

00:19:50.290 --> 00:19:51.250
Now!

00:20:03.800 --> 00:20:04.680
Ringo!

00:20:18.820 --> 00:20:20.400
Don't let go.

00:20:30.660 --> 00:20:31.450
Okay.

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:36.130
Heave...

00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:37.630
ho!

00:20:39.710 --> 00:20:41.130
I want a cola!

00:20:41.130 --> 00:20:42.520
Get me an orange juice.

00:20:42.520 --> 00:20:45.300
I-I'll hab the shame...

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:47.680
Here. Here.

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:54.530
Golly, that Distribution teacher's
a fine feller if there ever was one!

00:20:54.530 --> 00:20:59.320
Takin' us on a trip to the beach
as thanks for protectin' the paddy!

00:21:01.280 --> 00:21:02.030
That's for sure.

00:21:02.030 --> 00:21:05.650
I can finally see the ocean
what I've been hankerin' for!

00:21:05.650 --> 00:21:07.990
Even our school can be
magnanimous at times.

00:21:08.390 --> 00:21:12.050
I must say, Kousaku, you're lucky you got away with a reprimand.

00:21:12.050 --> 00:21:12.950
That's for sure.

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:16.670
One misstep and you'd have
both been suspended.

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:21.920
I wouldn't necessarily mind that.

00:21:31.510 --> 00:21:33.270
Uh-oh, Kousaku.

00:21:33.640 --> 00:21:36.390
I was just listening to the radio...

00:21:36.390 --> 00:21:38.350
The typhoon that is about to make landfall

00:21:38.350 --> 00:21:42.230
is of a magnitude that dwarfs
the recent Typhoon Number 9.

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:46.450
Winds near the eye of the storm are expected to reach 45 meters per second.

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:49.280
Beach!

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:50.910
Calm down, Minori!

00:21:50.910 --> 00:21:52.370
Wanna go beach! <i>Wanna go beach</i>!

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:53.700
S-Somebody stop her!

00:21:53.700 --> 00:21:54.660
Right!

00:21:54.660 --> 00:21:56.660
Come on, Mino-poyo!

00:21:57.670 --> 00:21:59.460
Beach Boys!

00:21:59.460 --> 00:22:00.880
You're a <i>girl</i>!

00:23:37.290 --> 00:23:39.980
"The Vegetable Battle of Ultimate and Supreme!"
